<article class="env-remark" id="02TU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02TU">Remark <span data-tag="02TU">42.32.3</span>.</a> We will see later (Lemma <a href="/tag/02TY" data-tag="02TY">42.36.3</a>) that if $X$ is a vector bundle of rank $r$ over $Y$ then the pullback map $\mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(Y) \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k + r}(X)$ is an isomorphism. This is true whenever $X \to Y$ satisfies the assumptions of Lemma <a href="/tag/02TT" data-tag="02TT">42.32.1</a>, see <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Lemma 2.2</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Totaro-group">Totaro-group</a>]</span>. We will sketch a proof in Remark <a href="/tag/0GUB" data-tag="0GUB">42.32.8</a> using higher chow groups. </p>
</article>